  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nBrisk northwest flow aloft will accompany a couple of disturbances\nstarting early Monday morning and continuing through Monday night. \nThe highest instability is expected to the west of our area, however \nthere may be a few isolated to scattered storms developing in \nassociation with the weak energy aloft. The best chance for these \nscattered storms will be early Monday morning across our western and \nsouthwestern counties, then again in the late evening Monday area \nwide. By late Monday night there will likely be a more significant \nwell- organized cluster or line of storms originating over the Great \nLakes moving southeast through the middle Ohio Valley. With some \nmodest overnight instability and 40 knots of bulk shear, damaging \nwinds will be the primary threat. Also can't rule out locally heavy \nrain with the most intense storms.\n\nA cold front on Tuesday will end the storm threat and bring near\nnormal to slightly below normal temperatures back into the area for\nthe rest of the week.",
